= Dataset — Simple =

A dataset is an organized collection of related data treated as a unit for storage, analysis, exchange, citation, or reuse.

A dataset can contain raw observations, processed measurements, derived variables, annotations, simulation outputs, survey responses, images, sequences, tables, or other structured records.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* dataset ≠ database
* dataset ≠ raw data necessarily

